  "body": "Closes #1205\nClaim: mac/mac-mbp\nAuthor model: Opus 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-w1205)\n\nLOT-067 (follow-up; not a lot PR).\n\n### Problem\n`LegacyAccountArchive.decode` read the legacy `HFR_COMPTES_KEY` archive with `requiresSecureCoding = false`, so the archive could name any class (#1205). #1202 tried secure coding with a class list and was reverted (`7b2ca13`): \"decodes every field of the legacy archive\" failed with `sourceUnreadable`.\n\n### Cause (measured on macOS 27.2)\n- `NSHTTPCookie` does not adopt `NSSecureCoding`: `unarchivedObject(ofClasses:from:)` with #1202's list throws `Class 'NSHTTPCookie' does not adopt it` (code 4864). No class list can include it.\n- `plutil -p` of the replayed archive (`MultisManager.m:49-80` @ `87fe0d1c`): `$classes` = `NSArray`, `NSMutableDictionary`, `NSHTTPCookie`, `NSDate`; strings, numbers and data inline. Each `NSHTTPCookie` archives one object, its properties dictionary, as the unkeyed `$0` (keys `Domain`, `Created`, `Secure`, `Expires`, `Path`, `Name`, `Value`, plus `HttpOnly` when set).\n- Same on the iOS 27.0 simulator (probe binaries run with `simctl spawn`): same refusal of `NSHTTPCookie`, same `$classes`, same `$0` layout. The substitute decode and the forged-`$0` refusals behave identically.\n\n### Change\n- Secure decoding with `allowedClasses` = `NSArray`, `NSDictionary`, `NSString`, `NSNumber`, `NSData`, `NSDate`, `NSURL`, plus `LegacyArchivedCookie`.\n- `setClass(LegacyArchivedCookie.self, forClassName: \"NSHTTPCookie\")`. This internal `NSSecureCoding` class reads the `$0` dictionary with an unkeyed `decodeObject()`, which inherits the unarchiver's allowed classes (checked: a forged `$0` holding another class fails the whole decode, and a non-secure class in it is never instantiated). The cookie is then rebuilt with `HTTPCookie(properties:)`. `NSHTTPCookie` itself is never instantiated from the archive.\n- An unarchiver error is `sourceUnreadable`. The rest of `decode` is unchanged.\n- LOT-067 spec: an Intentional differences entry (the reason and the measurements). M1 is reworded: the real-item check stays.\n\n### Tests\n- `unexpectedClass` (new): an archive whose account dictionary holds a test class outside the list → `sourceUnreadable`, and that class's `init(coder:)` never runs. **Red before the change** (no error thrown, class instantiated: 2 issues).\n- `forgedCookie` (new): an archive whose `NSHTTPCookie` `$0` holds a class outside the list → `sourceUnreadable`. It passed before the change too (the real `NSHTTPCookie` rejects that dictionary). It guards the substitute's unkeyed read.\n- `decode` (widened): domain, path, value, `Secure` and `HttpOnly` survive the rebuild. The fixture now sets `Secure`/`HttpOnly` only when true: Foundation reads them by presence, so `\"FALSE\"` counted as set.\n- `swift test --filter HFRStorageTests` on macOS: 571 tests pass.\n\nNo `### Ledger` section: no user-visible legacy behaviour changes for a legacy-written archive.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFeNfBA416G5kNZLfw\n\n",
